items.source:
AssertJ based JSON tester that works with basic JSON strings. Allows testing of JSON
payloads created from any source, for example:<pre class="code">public class ExampleObjectJsonTests {

    private BasicJsonTester json = new BasicJsonTester(getClass());

    @Test
    public void testWriteJson() throws IOException {
        assertThat(json.from("example.json")).extractingJsonPathStringValue("@.name")
                        .isEqualTo("Spring");
    }

}
</pre>

See <a href="AbstractJsonMarshalTester.html" title="class in org.springframework.boot.test.json"><code>AbstractJsonMarshalTester</code></a> for more details.

